WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.502
- Because of the
work that I've done

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
on these issues protecting
women and girls,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.975 align:start size:88% position:13%
I have heard from people
about scholarships,

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:13.847
academic competitions, I've
heard about job promotions.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:17.784 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have even had cases
in women's prisons

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:22.522 align:start size:97% position:3%
and domestic abuse shelters
where someone presents

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:27.527
and says they're a female
or they identify as female.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.498
So you are so correct on this.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:35.502
It is something that
is becoming an issue

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:39.973
in so many different
areas of our society.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:44.077
And people want to
make certain that

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
what they have fought
for, the rights,

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start size:97% position:3%
the opportunities they
have fought for as a woman,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.155
that those are recognized

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:58.425
and that they are
not disadvantaged.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.927
(mellow music)

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.002
is the senior US Senator

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the great
state of Tennessee,

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.706
and somebody who actually
knows what a woman is.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.208
How wild.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.877 align:start size:97% position:3%
Senator Marsha Blackburn,
welcome to the Rubin Report.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.179
- It is good to be with you.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.246
Thank you.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.682
- So I wanna start right there.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.451
You know what a woman is,

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.619
and not only do you
know what a woman is,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.788
you've asked other people,

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:84% position:16%
in this case then
Supreme Court nominee

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.227
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.230
You asked her what a woman
was a couple months back

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.698
in a very viral clip.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to throw to that
and get your thoughts.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.471 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Can you provide a
definition for the word woman?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.774
- Can I provide a definition?

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.608
No.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.609
- [Marsha] Mm-hm, yeah.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.044
- I can't.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.045
- [Marsha] You can't?

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.982
- Not in this context.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.484
I'm not a biologist.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.252
- So you believe the meaning
of the word woman is so unclear

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:03.356
and controversial that you
can't give me a definition.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.126
- Senator, in my
work as a judge,

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:10.563
what I do is I address disputes.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.700
If there's a dispute
about a definition,

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.537
people make arguments and I
look at the law and I decide.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.072
So I'm not...

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:23.409
- The fact that you can't
give me a straight answer

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:27.647 align:start size:97% position:3%
about something as
fundamental as what a woman is

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
underscores the
dangers of the kind

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:34.954
of progressive education
that we are hearing about.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:40.059 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, senator, did you
expect that sort of response?

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.561
- You know, I did not.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.931
And when you look at the
full line of questioning,

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
I started with the school
board she serves on

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:51.638
and the fact that they have a
woke kindergarten curriculum,

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.773
did she support that?

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.575 align:start size:84% position:16%
She said she didn't
know about it.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:03:00.513
So I asked her about Virginia
and VMI and that case made it

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:05.285
to the Supreme Court,
US versus Virginia.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.954 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that is the decision
that was written

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
by Ruth Bader Ginsburg
that allowed women

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.425
into our military academies,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.762
and it's kind of law
school first year.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I asked if she
agreed with Ginsburg

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:22.502
and her writing and gave
her that quote and said

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:26.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
it basically said women and
men have enduring differences.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well, she said she
had never heard

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:32.412 align:start size:97% position:3%
of the case and was
unfamiliar with the writing.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.415
I didn't think that
sounded quite right.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:39.652 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I asked her to
define the word woman

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:43.990
and she refused to
do so, as we've seen.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I did that because
I was trying to get

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:50.697 align:start size:97% position:3%
to men in women's sports and
the impact that is having

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:54.534
on young women, and just
like US versus Virginia,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:59.405
I know that at some point
what the NCAA has done

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:03.276
with allowing men in women's
sports, there will be lawsuits

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.845
and that will make its
way to the Supreme Court.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.614
So I wanted to see
where she was on it.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.749 align:start size:84% position:16%
And Dave, you know
the interesting thing,

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:14.754
I met privately with her
before we did our hearings.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.192
I laid out for her
when we met privately

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.595
what I was going to ask
her about when we did go

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.030
into the hearing.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.932
We had a delightful discussion.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.234
We met for about an hour.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.336
We went through a
series of things

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:34.674
and I was very fair pointing
out what I was going to ask.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:37.844
Then when we did our
opening statements

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:42.315 align:start size:97% position:3%
on Monday prior to the
hearing beginning on Tuesday,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:46.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
I again went
through a recitation

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.822
listing the things I
was going to discuss

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:52.225 align:start size:81% position:19%
with her in the
committee setting.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.661
So she knew what was coming

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:58.965
but she chose not to
give me an answer.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:03.903
And everyone knows that there
are differences between men

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:09.042 align:start position:0%
and women, and I think everybody
could give me a definition

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a woman, an adult
female, two X chromosomes.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.883
I think that there are plenty

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:21.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
of ways that this
could be answered,
saying, "I am a woman."

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.956
There are ways to answer that.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:28.628
So it just shows you how
far the left is pushing

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:33.333
even members of the US
Supreme Court to deny

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:37.337
that there are differences
between male and female.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:40.239
- You know, I hate to play
the identity politics game,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:43.910 align:start size:97% position:3%
but for you as a female
senator asking this question,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.814
how concerned are you now
that as these cases rise up

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.515
to the Supreme Court

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:53.019
that they will not
have a foundational
definition of woman?

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
And as you say, I mean,
we already have it.

00:05:55.888 --> 00:06:00.126 align:start size:97% position:3%
We will have men beating
women in collegiate swimming,

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.995 align:start size:97% position:3%
in wrestling, in basketball,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.098
And although it's just in
some sense, people think,

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.499
"Oh, well, that's
just about sports."

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.368 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's actually about something
much bigger happening

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.069
in society right now.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:13.673
- Well, it is, and because
of the work that I've done

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:18.111
on these issues protecting
women and girls, I have heard

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:22.582 align:start position:0%
from people about scholarships,
academic competitions.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:25.385
I've heard about job promotions.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:29.322 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have even had cases
in women's prisons

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:34.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
and domestic abuse shelters
where someone presents

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:39.031
and says they're a female
or they identify as female.

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.969
So you are so correct on this.

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:46.939
It is something that
is becoming an issue

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:51.477
in so many different
areas of our society.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:55.982
And people want to
make certain that

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:59.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
what they have fought
for, the rights,

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:03.689 align:start size:97% position:3%
the opportunities they
have fought for as a woman,

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.559
that those are recognized

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:09.695
and that they are
not disadvantaged.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're going to continue
to stay on this issue

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:18.271 align:start size:97% position:3%
and continue to support
women and girls as they work

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.874
to preserve the opportunities
that should be there for them.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:23.709 align:start size:97% position:3%
- One more on this and then
we'll get to some other stuff.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:24.944
Do your colleagues

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:28.014
on the other side of
this issue, you know,

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:31.284 align:start size:97% position:3%
generally Democrats consider
themselves feminists,

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:35.221
so that means that they would
be for women in some sense.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:38.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do any of them when you
talk to them privately, say,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.793
"Boy, we've really
kind of lost the ball

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
on this one and we're
actually defending men who

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.667
purport to be women, let's say,

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:50.303
but it's sort of gone too far."

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:52.138
The whole party has
gone so radical,

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:54.207
there's not much
that they can do.

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:56.776 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You know, one of
the interesting things

00:07:56.776 --> 00:08:01.714 align:start size:97% position:3%
to me has been how women on
the left will all fall in line

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:08.688
behind whatever the left says
is their agenda for women.

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.492 align:start size:81% position:19%
And they stay very
close to that.

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:17.497
They're very submissive to
the left's agenda on gender.

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:22.468
But when you have
conservative women

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.537
or women that are center right

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:26.973
or to the right,
what do you hear?

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:31.711
They will come at you and
will absolutely blast you

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:34.180 align:start size:84% position:16%
and say, "Oh, you're
not a real woman.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.516
Oh, you're not defending women."

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:39.952
If you don't fall
in line and submit

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.687
to that agenda to the left.

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:46.359
It is a very interesting
dynamic that is happening.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:49.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
And these leftist groups,
they don't show up

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:52.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
to protect women who
are conservative.

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.800
- So I saw you a
couple weeks ago.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.369
You were kind enough
to take a few minutes

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:59.405
in your office right
after the midterms.

00:08:59.405 --> 00:09:02.475
And obviously the red
wave did not fully form

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:04.310
the way a lot of people thought.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.379
And when we were chatting

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:07.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
they were still
trying to figure out

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.715
even if the Republicans
were gonna get Congress,

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:11.951
which obviously did happen.

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.185
Are you hopeful now

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:15.721 align:start size:88% position:13%
that there's gonna be
some actual change here?

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:16.989
I mean, I think a lot of people,

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:18.991 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I know this from
my own audience,

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:21.260
they're happy that the
Republicans got Congress

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.429 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there's always this
feeling like, ah, they got it,

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.965
but are they gonna
actually do anything?

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:27.934
- And one of the frustrations

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:30.736 align:start size:88% position:13%
for so many Tennesseans
that I talked to

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:34.840 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that you have Republicans
who will not back

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.444
Republican principles and
they want them to focus

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:41.147
on getting the government
spending under control,

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:44.450
securing that southern
border, making certain

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:48.621
that crime is addressed,
that we work to get drugs

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:51.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
off the street and
support law enforcement.

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:53.392
Those are the things

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:56.529 align:start size:88% position:13%
that people are wanting
to see addressed.

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:58.898
And they're very concerned

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:03.269
that you will have
some Republicans in
the House and some

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:07.506
in the Senate that won't
support getting things done

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:09.208
for the American people.

00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.210
I fully believe

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.814
that this next two years
is a great opportunity

00:10:14.814 --> 00:10:19.752
for Republicans to
show what we are for

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:22.388
and to draw that distinction

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:26.492
between what Democrats are for
and what Republicans are for.

00:10:26.492 --> 00:10:28.527
It's a great opportunity for us.

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:31.764
We should embrace that
and we should be bold.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.933
- So, are you hopeful that
the Congress will do it?

00:10:33.933 --> 00:10:36.068
Obviously, you don't have as
much leverage in the Senate,

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:39.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
but do you think that
whoever ends up as the leader

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.174
and whatever direction they
go will be the right one?

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:47.913 align:start size:97% position:3%
- My hope is that you're
going to see House Republicans

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:51.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
and Senate Republicans
work together to stop a lot

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:55.287 align:start size:88% position:13%
of these bad initiatives
that are coming

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.856
out of the White House.

00:10:56.856 --> 00:11:00.226
And we need to be sure we
don't make life difficult

00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:04.096
for one another, but that
we stay focused on things,

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:07.299 align:start size:97% position:3%
A few things that the American
people want to see done.

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:10.603
The spending, the
crime, the border,

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:13.506
making certain we
fund the military,

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:17.476
making certain that we are
protecting our families.

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:18.911
- Let me ask you a little bit

00:11:18.911 --> 00:11:21.113 align:start size:97% position:3%
about your home state of
Tennessee, because Tennessee,

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:24.750
much like Florida, where I am
now, is absolutely booming.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I told you I
considered Nashville.

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:29.021
It almost happened,

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:30.656 align:start size:88% position:13%
but a lot of my friends
have moved there.

00:11:30.656 --> 00:11:32.391
As you know, Daily Wire
has moved down there.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:35.594
There's really like
a real explosion in
Tennessee right now.

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:36.829
Are you guys just feeling good

00:11:36.829 --> 00:11:38.197
about things, like,
we're doing it right?

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:41.233 align:start size:88% position:13%
We're seeing this influx
and it's all good?

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:45.771
- Yes, but bear in mind
this has been a long time

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:49.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the making, getting
Tennessee on the right path.

00:11:49.909 --> 00:11:52.978 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I was in the State
Senate, there was a big push

00:11:52.978 --> 00:11:57.349
and it was a four year
battle, four full years.

00:11:57.349 --> 00:12:00.753
We had a governor that was
pushing a state income tax

00:12:00.753 --> 00:12:02.788
and I led that opposition.

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:06.058
We kept our state
income tax-free.

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:09.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're never going
to have a income tax

00:12:09.495 --> 00:12:11.464 align:start size:84% position:16%
in Tennessee because
we've amended

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:15.601
the State Constitution
that doesn't allow it.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.903
- What was the argument for it?

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:21.540
It seems so hard for me as
a former Californian to come

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.242
to Florida where I'm
paying no income tax.

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:25.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
The idea that anyone
here would say,

00:12:25.277 --> 00:12:27.646
"Yes, we would like
income tax here."

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:29.749
It just sounds so insane.

00:12:29.749 --> 00:12:34.754 align:start position:0%
- Yes, and Tennessee in the
mid '90s had been the test case

